KG42.register("clusters-05edca5bf3faf80ecf843119",{"id":"38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v142-d-K005","paper":"38-bidirectional_ev_trading","label":"Collaborative welfare objective and aggregator responsibilities under bounded load uncertainty","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K005","label":"Collaborative welfare objective and aggregator responsibilities under bounded load uncertainty","market_meaning":"Under bounded load disturbance conditions, customer scheduling targets the worst actual social welfare; the aggregator approves or at least knows the disturbance bounds and undertakes the responsibility of calculating the worst disturbance round by round. The objective, bounds, and responsibility can be connected, but the worst-case calculation and distributed updates have not yet formed closed rules.","mechanism_ids":["M03"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","coordination"],"scope_disposition":"compatible","scope_explanation":"Both Rule-Chains belong to the robust collaboration mechanism and use system actual welfare and the common bounded disturbance context. Only the uncertainty set boundary and the calculation responsibility are connected; M04's worst disturbance for each customer's payoff is not introduced, nor is M01's deterministic object identity borrowed.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The disturbance boundary is an input to the robust objective, and the aggregator's calculation of the worst case is the corresponding responsible activity, so this is assembled across settlement and coordination. The ambiguity in calculation direction and information indexing in the source remains unresolved, and the responsibility statement cannot be presented as a closed algorithm.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R011","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide actual welfare, the disturbance set, and the robust collaborative objective."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R012","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the approval or knowledge requirement for the disturbance bounds, and the aggregator's responsibility to calculate the worst disturbance round by round."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K005-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R012","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R011","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-T03","v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-T04","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15"],"rationale":"The same source explicitly uses the upper and lower bounds approved or known by the aggregator for the uncertainty set of the robust objective; this interface does not copy parameter objects in R012."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K005-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R011","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R012","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-X03","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e21"],"rationale":"The inner layer of the robust objective needs to evaluate the worst actual welfare, and the source assigns the round-by-round worst disturbance calculation to the aggregator. Here the objective use and the responsible activity are connected, and no ambiguous calculation formula or communication summation formula is supplied."}],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K005-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Equation (20) of B defines the worst disturbance as minimizing actual welfare, while the quotation for Equation (21) shows maximization; there is a conflict in calculation direction. The robust minimization objective of frozen R011 remains as it is, and the calculation responsibility of R012 cannot on this basis be supplemented into an unambiguous calculation rule.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R011","v141-c-R012"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C004","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e21"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Trace back to original Equations (20) and (21) and the context to verify the direction, and then upstream supplements a citable worst-case calculation Rule-Chain; D does not change signs on its own."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K005-G02","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"e21 calls the disturbance aggregate the sum of other customers, but the displayed index includes all customers. At present it cannot be determined whether the transmitted total includes this customer, nor can the combination of the received quantity and the local disturbance be determined on that basis.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R012"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the original text, the displayed index, and the communication object; before this customer is clearly excluded or included, do not add a new information quantity identity mapping or graph edge."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K005-G03","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The existing Rule-Chain does not carry the complete projection updates of Equations (22) to (24), nor does it expand X_i; the objective and calculation responsibility cannot replace the complete distributed robust scheduling process.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R011","v141-c-R012"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-T05","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C004","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e21"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream supplements the projection updates, feasible sets, and information interface Rule-Chains of the same mechanism, and after the algorithm conditions are clarified, checks process closure."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K005-G04","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The bounded load disturbance set is currently attached to the welfare node, and the related uncertainty node proposal has still not been approved.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R011","v141-c-R012"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C003","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e16"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g02-p02"],"required_work":"Manual inspection should examine whether the proposal requires an independent ontology representation; before approval, keep the existing welfare node and boundary parameter references."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K005-G05","category":"unverified_source","description":"The disturbance definition, robust objective, calculation direction, and communication description all come from B material that has not been independently audited, and its current source_status remains unchanged.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R011","v141-c-R012"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e21"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently check the original formulas and communication paragraphs item by item, distinguish transcription problems from original mathematical problems; do not treat candidate assembly as passing independent review."}]},"rule_refs":["38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R011","38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R012"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-ebacec241379c91d","KG40-88d16cf517d0bffb"]});
